    "notes": "Voxel metrics, not skeleton ones: these volumes ship dense label arrays and no skeletons, so nERL is\nunavailable and panoptic quality ranks. Not comparable with any NISB nERL figure, nor with\nlmd_ssl_v1_neuron_instance, which averages four volumes per half.\n\nOne volume per half. The fit half is zebrafish_fish2_quadcube1 (4.247 G voxels scored), the reported\nhalf zebrafish_fish2_doublecube1 (7.078 G). Both sit on a 1920-cubed lattice at 8.0/8.0/8.027 nm,\nidentical for all three arms -- verified from each artifact's own native_box, read_shape and\neffective_voxel_nm rather than assumed from the config.\n\nLabels are 1..k with no background: mutex watershed assigns every voxel to a cluster. Ids are\ncompacted at conversion because `_factorize` only takes its counting path while the id span stays\nunder 2**31, and these two volumes carry raw union-find root ids spanning 4.2 G and 7.06 G.\n"
  },
